# KB Connector Helper — Environment Variable Overrides (optional)
#
# ── Purpose ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file documents the environment variables the tool honors. It is the
# SECONDARY, optional configuration mechanism — most users never need it.
#
#   • kb-connector.toml   → PRIMARY config. Defines your connectors and defaults
#                           (see kb-connector.example.toml). This is what you
#                           edit day-to-day or generate with `kb-connector init`.
#
#   • environment vars    → OPTIONAL low-priority fallback. Useful in CI or for
#                           one-off overrides without editing the TOML. They only
#                           fill values the TOML doesn't provide.
#
# Resolution precedence (highest wins):
#   CLI flag  >  [connectors.<name>]  >  [defaults]  >  environment variable
#
# So a value in kb-connector.toml ALWAYS beats the matching environment variable.
# There is no conflict between the two files — the TOML wins.
#
# ── Not auto-loaded ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tool does NOT read this .env file automatically. To use these, export them
# into your shell (`export AWS_REGION=us-west-2`) or have your CI inject them as
# environment variables. Copying this file to `.env` alone does nothing.
#
# ── Honored variables (this is the complete list the code reads) ─────────────

# AWS region for all AWS calls (overridden by [defaults].region or --region).
# AWS_REGION=us-west-2

# Named AWS credentials profile (overridden by [defaults].profile or --profile).
# AWS_PROFILE=my-profile

# Microsoft Entra tenant ID for SharePoint/OneDrive (overridden by
# [defaults.microsoft].tenant_id, [connectors.<name>].tenant_id, or --tenant-id).
# AZURE_TENANT_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-4xxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
